  "historical_output_text": " Context: Learning basic first aid\n\nQ. Hi I’m new, what’s a must-need thing to keep when you learn about doing First-Hand for emergencies in my apartment?\nA Sure question to start learning basic First Aid skills. A well-thanked first item should certainly include an Emergency Medic Kit or \"first-need kit.\"\n\nIn the case apartment living or any space, it would do good to stock the basics:\n\n**First-Area Kits**\n- Band AID strips: Various widths & length.\n   *Caut: Avoid super strong adhesive that might hurt in removal* .\n- Adhesive plasteer: Great to use to cover blazes, blurs.\n   \n- Antibacterial creams/goo: Essential if the area has open blazes. Helps to reduce bacteria that might grow.\n  \n   *Wrt. tip:",
